Helios vkd3d-proton fork: admission polling, barrier pass-end statistics

Conduit Basemark D3D12 on NVK (398.1): commit-to-admission averages
1.85 ms per batch with the GPU about half busy, and 61.7k of 75.4k passes
per 2 s are ended by ResourceBarrier. Applied after 0007.

- HELIOS_VKD3D_ADMISSION_SPIN_US (default 0): the submission worker polls a
  batch's admission event for that long (WaitForSingleObject(0) with
  YieldProcessor, clamped to 20 ms) before blocking on it, to take the
  thread wake out of the admission chain. Logged once when on.
- With HELIOS_VKD3D_PASS_END_STATS=1 the two-second window also gets one
  "ResourceBarrier" line: calls, barriers asked for, calls that ended an
  active render pass, how many of those emitted no Vulkan barrier at all
  (ended the pass for nothing), and the Vulkan image and memory barriers
  made. (A batch flushed half-way at MAX_BATCHED_IMAGE_BARRIERS counts only
  its tail; transitions emitted outside the batch are not seen.)

